{"text": "TIME LINE OF SOME EVENTS\nIN HISTORY OF S21\n\n1989 Beckett Chapter 13 Bankruptcy #89-53934-JS\n\n2/1/90 \u201cThe Washington Executive Group, Inc.\u201d in operation. Ken Lines\u2019 is\na registered agent. Lines later became the company\u2019s insurance agent and\nmuch later claimed that Beckett had taken him for $95,000. in this venture.\nLines claimed that Beckett wrote this off in a bankruptcy. Kerr\u2019s office is\nshown as the address. -\n\n1991 Beckett Chapter 7 Bankruptcy #91-5-7123-JS\n\n5/10/94 Letter to Dan D\u2019aniello of Carlyle Group from Richard Beckett\nlooking for start up funds for new security company. \u2018 / / -2\n\n5/11/94 Fax from USSS Financial Crimes Division/Forgery to Beckett re\ncredit report on Richard Werner and March 15\" invoice to same. This is\n\nalmost certainly from Rakowski. 94-\n\n6/15/94 Letter to Dan D\u2019aniello from Richard Beckett discussing joint\nventure with General Bloomer of American Protective Services. - 7 \u00a2 \u201c5\n\n6/15/94 Fax from USS Technical Security Division to Richard Beckett at the\nWhite House. This is a credit report on American Protective Services / Y by\n\nMid 1994 Dodd is believed to have met Beckett\n\n9/16/94 Fax from Dan D\u2019aniello to BDM to discuss BDM / BBI security\nventure. u -/)\n\n9/20/94 Letter to Dan D\u2019aniello from BDM concerning BBI venture. - aq Y-\u00a5\n\n9/21/94 Fax to Richard Beckett from Dan D\u2019aniello concerning BDM\nresponse. a Y -G\n\nLate 1994 Dodd briefly meets Paul Rakowski, just retired from Secret\nService, who was introduced by Beckett in an Easton restaurant.\n\n{B0353592:1} 1",
